Z||000000||Elenor84||11-30-2000||05:09 PM||||Hey guys I just bought this fiero and there is no keys for the deck that the other ppl installed...what do u suggest?  It is a pioneer deck...if u need serial number just ask...thx!<P>------------------<BR>Lance||||reg||1
Z||000001||Raydar||11-30-2000||05:47 PM||||Are you talking about a removable face plate that's missing?<BR>If you have a model and serial number, you can probably get one from Pioneer. I would expect that they are <I>not</I> inexpensive, though.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Fiero_Freak||11-30-2000||08:55 PM||||Do you mean the "keys" you still in the sides to withdrawl the head unit from the sleeve?||||reg||1
Z||000003||Seanh||11-30-2000||10:14 PM||||If you are talking about the "keys" to remove the deck from the mounting plate. Just unscrew the trim panel and remove the whole thing if you really need to take it out. I dont know what else you could be talking about, please let us know.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/transsig.gif">   <BR><A HREF="http://www.kdsi.net/~sean" TARGET=_blank>Sean's Fiero Page</A><BR>Sean Heberly<BR>Silver 86 GT 2.8 Auto<BR>Going on to 3.4 in Jan.<BR><I>"It's always in the last place you look." Of course it is. Why would you keep looking after you've found it? Do people do this? Who and where are they?</I>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Elenor84||12-01-2000||02:47 AM||||Yes thats right...to remove the whole thing...I need to find a wire and there's to many back there to see...so I need to take it out...so how do I go about taking it out?<P>------------------<BR>Lance||||reg||1
Z||000005||Seanh||12-01-2000||05:19 PM||||Just remove the trim panel, it has 4 torx screws, one on each corner. Then remove the 9/32" screws holding the mounting plate to the metal brace behind it, there should be 4 screws. Then pull the stereo out slowly and unplug the connectors and antenna. Thats all there is to it.||||reg||1
